---
/** A diagram of the three levels a BEAM model can describe. Static: no data. */
---

<figure class="levels not-content" aria-label="Three levels of BEAM model: one per repertoire, one per group, and a reference over all groups">
	<div class="level">
		<div class="title">One repertoire</div>
		<div class="reps">
			<span class="rep a">R1</span>
		</div>
		<div class="arrow">↓ build</div>
		<div class="model a">model of R1</div>
		<p>Describes one sample or one person. Compare samples, follow a person over time, plan the depth for this sample.</p>
	</div>
	<div class="level">
		<div class="title">One group</div>
		<div class="reps">
			<span class="rep b">R1</span><span class="rep b">R2</span><span class="rep b">R3</span>
		</div>
		<div class="arrow">↓ pool the cells, then build</div>
		<div class="model b">model of the group</div>
		<p>
			Describes a cell type, a condition or a cohort. Compare groups, ask which group a sequence resembles,
			predict sharing within the group.
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="level">
		<div class="title">Everything: a reference</div>
		<div class="reps">
			<span class="rep a">…</span><span class="rep b">…</span><span class="rep c">…</span><span class="rep a">…</span>
		</div>
		<div class="arrow">↓ pool all, then build</div>
		<div class="model c">reference model</div>
		<p>
			Generalises over all the data given, like the foundation model built from 38,538 repertoires. The baseline
			for "how likely in people in general".
		</p>
	</div>
</figure>

<style>
	.levels {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(13rem, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
		margin: 1.5rem 0;
	}
	.level {
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		padding: 0.9rem;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		align-content: start;
		text-align: center;
	}
	.title {
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.reps {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: center;
		gap: 0.3rem;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
	}
	.rep {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
		padding: 0.15rem 0.45rem;
		border-radius: 0.3rem;
		border: 1px solid currentColor;
	}
	.arrow {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}
	.model {
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		padding: 0.35rem;
		border-radius: 0.35rem;
		color: var(--sl-color-black);
	}
	.a {
		color: var(--sl-color-accent);
	}
	/* text colours with at least 4.5:1 contrast on each theme's background */
	.levels {
		--ml-b: #ef785f;
		--ml-c: #9aa4ea;
	}
	:global(:root[data-theme='light']) .levels {
		--ml-b: #b5472f;
		--ml-c: #4b5cc4;
	}
	.b {
		color: var(--ml-b);
	}
	.c {
		color: var(--ml-c);
	}
	.model.a {
		background: var(--sl-color-accent);
		color: var(--sl-color-black);
	}
	.model.b {
		background: #ef785f;
		color: #16314b;
	}
	.model.c {
		background: #4b5cc4;
		color: #fff;
	}
	.level p {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
		margin: 0;
		text-align: left;
	}
</style>
